    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[Differentiate the following function with respect to x
\(F(x)=\displaystyle\int_{{@lb@}}^{{@ub@}}{@f@} dt\) <br><br>

<table>
<tr>
<td>The function can be differentiated using [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]]</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>with condition [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</td>
</tr>
</table>

<table>
<tr>
 <td>we use the [[input:ans3]] since one limit of integration is [[input:ans4]] <td>
 [[validation:ans3]][[validation:ans4]]</td>
</tr>
</table>

<table>
<tr>
 <td>Let [[input:ans5]]  \(\implies\) [[input:ans6]]<br>
[[validation:ans5]][[validation:ans6]]</td>
 </tr>
 </table><br>
 
 Using the above theorems the derivative is given by
 <table>
 <tr>
 <td>\(\displaystyle\frac{d}{dx}\left(\int_{{@lb@}}^{{@ub@}}{@f@} dt\right)=\) [[input:ans7]]  \(\times\) [[input:ans8]]<br>
 [[validation:ans7]][[validation:ans8]]</td>
 </tr>
 </table><br>
substituting the value for \(u\),
 <table>
 <tr>
<td>\(\displaystyle\frac{d}{dx}\left(\int_{{@lb@}}^{{@ub@}}{@f@} dt\right)=\) [[input:ans9]] [[validation:ans9]]</td>
</tr>
</table>
[[feedback:prt1]]]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<i style="color:green"><b>FUNDAMENTAL THEOREM OF CALCULUS: </b>
<br>If \(f\) is a continuous function on \([a,b]\)   then the function  \(F\)  defined by  \(F(x) =\displaystyle \int_{a}^{x}f(t)dt\) is differentiable on \((a,b)\) and its derivative is given by  \(F'(x)=f(x)\).

<b>CHAIN RULE </b><br>
The derivative of a composite function \(y=f(u)\) and \(u=g(x)\) is given by 
\[\frac{dy}{dx}=\frac{dy}{du}\times\frac{du}{dx}\]
 </i>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
